dew:
Softly, O softly we bear her along,
She hangs like a star in the dew of our song;
She springs like a beam on the brow of the tide,

dewdrops:
Be the green grass above me
With showers and dewdrops wet;
And if thou wilt, remember,

dewfall:
The wealth of our valleys, new-garnered and ripe;
O sender of rain and the dewfall, we hail thee,
We praise thee, Varuna, with cymbal and pipe.

dewed:
However shut up in the dark and dry;
But violets, aired and dewed by love like yours,
Out-smell all thyme! we keep that in our clothes,

She set it by a wall that faced the south;
Dewed it with tears, hoped for a root,
Watched for a waxing shoot,
